*External and internal applicants, as well as position incumbents, who are or become disabled as defined under the Americans with Disabilities Act or applicable state law, must be able to perform the essential functions of the job (including those listed above) either with or without reasonable accommodation. Reasonable accommodation, if any, will be determined by management in consultation with the employee on a case\\-by\\-case basis.*  



*This job description is intended to be general and may be revised from time to time. At management’s discretion, the employee may be assigned different or additional duties from time to time.*

**Primary Duties :**

* Responsible for providing services in the areas of Enterprise Performance Management, Business Intelligence applications implementations and software application design, development and integration;
* Performing the following: studying critical business processes and requirements, interacting with end users to gain an understanding of critical information needs and use Oracle and Data Integration technologies to develop custom BI applications;
* Customize packaged software solutions like Oracle Business Intelligence Applications, Hyperion Enterprise Performance Management, Oracle Information Discovery and Informatica to meet those needs;
* Conceptualize, design, construct, test, and deploy business and information technology solutions through the application of software development life cycle methodology appropriate to the specific enterprise application;
* Perform fit gap analysis of leading software packages like Oracle BI, Analytics, Informatica and Hyperion;
* Understand functional design and create technology architectures to facilitate implementations;
* Assist the application support team in analyzing and implementing application enhancements.

**Job Requirements :**

* Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Electronics and Communication Engineering, Information Technology, Computer Applications, or a related field of study required. Master’s preferred.
* Minimum 0\\-2 years related experience.
* Detail orientated with excellent time management skills.
* Excellent written and verbal communication skills.
* Experience with Data Analysis and Statistical Analysis.
* Strong knowledge of Tableau, SAS Programming, MySQL, NetBeans, Agile, MS Project, R Studio, SAS basics, HTML and UNIX.

**Primary Duties:**

* Providing expert services in the areas of Enterprise Performance Management and Business Intelligence applications implementations;
* Conducting business requirements analysis and review;
* Designing data integration and application architecture and components; implementing the application using the available integration frameworks;
